---
config:
  flowchart:
    rankSpacing: 30
---
flowchart TB
    accTitle: From pull requests to a published release
    accDescr: Pull requests titled fix, feat or feat! are merged into main, and the release bot keeps the pull request chore: release x.y.z with the version and the changelog. Once the maintainer merges it, a draft release with its tag is created, the package is built and checked, signed with the app's certificate, and gets its signature, SBOM and provenance. Then the release is published and immutable, delivered to the Nextcloud App Store, and verified, and every week again.

    subgraph request ["The release pull request"]
        direction TB
        prs["Pull requests<br>fix: · feat: · feat!:"] -- "merged<br>into main" --> bot["chore: release x.y.z<br>version and changelog"]
    end
    subgraph build ["Once the maintainer merges it"]
        direction TB
        draft["Draft release<br>with its tag"] --> package["Package built<br>and checked"] --> sign["Signed with the<br>app's certificate"] --> assets["Signature, SBOM,<br>provenance"]
    end
    subgraph publication ["Publication"]
        direction TB
        published["Release published,<br>immutable"] --> store["Nextcloud<br>App Store"] --> verify["Release verified,<br>and every week again"]
    end
    request --> build --> publication

    classDef person fill:#f59e0b2e,stroke:#f59e0b,stroke-width:2px
    classDef bot fill:#526cfe2e,stroke:#526cfe,stroke-width:2px
    classDef done fill:#16a34a2e,stroke:#16a34a,stroke-width:2px
    class prs person
    class bot,draft,package,sign,assets bot
    class published,store,verify done
